    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `customerCode` is a pure function of region + telephone + last name (computed in `BuildOwner`), so two distinct owners could in principle derive the same code. I added collision-driven de-duplication to the create-owner pipeline:\n\n1. **`CustomerCode.dedupe(String code, Set<String> existingCodes)`** \u2014 new static helper on the customer-code \"home\" class. If `code` collides with an existing owner's code, it appends `'-<n>'` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that yields a unique value; otherwise (or for `null`) it returns the code unchanged.\n\n2. **`DeduplicateCustomerCode`** \u2014 a new OfficeFloor function class that reads the built `@Val Owner`, gathers all other owners' customer codes from the `OwnerRepository` (skipping the same record by id), and stamps the de-duplicated code back onto the owner in place \u2014 so the response DTO, membership number, check digit and region all read from the single de-duplicated value.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `dedupeCustomerCode` step into the pipeline between `checkPossibleDuplicate` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours, following the project's function-injection conventions.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`) and the full build pass.",
